// One secrets file per App, named after its shell file. Copy this file and fill it in:
//
//   cp Config/Secrets/app.xcconfig.sample Config/Secrets/hope-tv-deutsch-tv-app.xcconfig
//   cp Config/Secrets/app.xcconfig.sample Config/Secrets/hope-tv.xcconfig
//
// Config/Shells/<app>.xcconfig includes Config/Secrets/<app>.xcconfig. Every other
// per-app key, the Entity id too, is in the shell file.
//
// The ClientToken is identity, not a secret: it ships readable inside the binary
// and the surface behind it is public content. It still never enters a tracked
// file — Config/Secrets/*.xcconfig is gitignored. Ask the Hope Platform team for an
// enabled `kind: 'app'` Client row of the App's environment (staging or production).

CLIENT_TOKEN = replace-me-with-real-client-token
